      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0031",
      "sequence": 886,
      "meaning": "Aṅgada says even that feat would bring no greatness, for killing one already dead shows no manhood. He lists fourteen living dead: one ruled by lust or a false vow, miserly, deluded, destitute, disgraced, very old, chronically ill, perpetually angry, turned from Viṣṇu, hostile to scripture and saints, body-obsessed, a slanderer and a mine of sin. Regarding Rāvaṇa thus, he refuses to kill him but warns him not to provoke anger. Grinding his teeth, Rāvaṇa says Aṅgada seeks death with a small mouth and large speech, relying on one without virtue or honour, exiled by his father and tormented by separation, whom demons eat daily.",
