    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0033",
      "sequence": 888,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa commands champions to devour every bear and monkey, clear Earth of them and take the two ascetic brothers alive. Aṅgada rebukes the shameless boaster: die after cutting your throat, thief of women and violator of households, heap of vice, lustful man-eater babbling under Time. Soon monkeys’ and bears’ slaps will repay these words. If Rāma were merely human, Rāvaṇa’s tongues would fall with his heads in battle. Rāma’s arrow-host thirsts for blood; only that fear keeps Aṅgada from killing the contemptible talker now. Blind with twenty eyes, Rāvaṇa cannot see that the one arrow which killed Bāli came from no ordinary man.",
