    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0034",
      "sequence": 889,
      "meaning": "Aṅgada says he is fit to break Rāvaṇa’s teeth but lacks Rāma’s command; otherwise he would tear off all ten mouths and sink Laṅkā in the sea. Laṅkā is a fig with Rāvaṇa and his creatures inside, and a monkey needs no time to eat such fruit, but generous Rāma forbade it. Rāvaṇa mocks him as a liar trained by ascetics. Aṅgada vows to tear out ten tongues unless that charge is true, then plants his foot in the court: if any demon can move it, Rāma will turn back and Sītā is lost. Indrajit and countless champions strain, fail and sit with bowed heads; the foot remains fixed like a saint’s mind against millions of obstacles.",
