    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0036",
      "sequence": 891,
      "meaning": "Mandodarī begs Rāvaṇa to abandon crooked thought: battle with Raghupati does not suit him. He could not cross even the small line drawn by Rāma’s younger brother, yet hopes to defeat the master of envoys who crossed the sea, entered Laṅkā, killed the guards and Akṣa before his eyes, ruined the grove and burned the city. He should stop empty boasting and know Rāma not as a king but as the unequalled Lord of moving and unmoving creation. Mārīca knew the arrows’ force; Rāvaṇa ignored him. In Janaka’s court Rāvaṇa stood among countless mighty kings when Rāma broke the bow and married Jānakī—why not defeat him then? Jayanta learned a fraction of his strength and lived only after losing an eye. Śūrpaṇakhā, Virādha, Khara, Dūṣaṇa, Kabandha and Bāli all testify.",
