      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0037",
      "sequence": 892,
      "meaning": "She continues: the compassionate banner of the solar line playfully bridged the sea and camped at Suvela, yet sent an envoy for Rāvaṇa’s good. In open court that envoy crushed his strength like a lion amid a herd, and Aṅgada and Hanumān are merely his servants. Why repeatedly call their master a man and cling vainly to honour, possession and pride? Time does not strike with a staff; it steals dharma, strength, intellect and judgment, producing delusion like Rāvaṇa’s. Two sons are dead and the city burned; even now he should return Sītā, worship compassionate Raghunātha and earn stainless fame.",
