    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0038",
      "sequence": 893,
      "meaning": "Mandodarī’s words strike like arrows, and at daybreak Rāvaṇa rises for council, sitting swollen with pride. Rāma summons Aṅgada, seats him nearby with honour and smilingly asks how he obtained four crowns from the immensely strong crest of the demon line. Aṅgada says they are not crowns but a king’s four virtues—conciliation, generosity, punishment and division. Veda says they dwell in a ruler’s heart; knowing Rāvaṇa to be without dharma, turned from the Lord and ruled by Time, they abandoned him and came to Rāma. Rāma smiles at the clever answer, and Aṅgada reports Laṅkā’s fortifications.",
