      "meaning": "On learning the enemy’s condition, Rāma summons his counsellors to decide how to assault Laṅkā’s four formidable gates. Sugrīva, Jāmbavān and Vibhīṣaṇa remember the solar dynasty’s ornament and divide the monkey host into four armies with fitting commanders. They summon every troop-leader and explain the Lord’s power. The monkeys bow at Rāma’s feet, seize mountain peaks and rush out roaring and threatening victory to Raghubīra. Knowing Laṅkā’s fortress is supreme yet fearless through Rāma, they surround all four sides in a dense mass and beat war-drums with their mouths.",
